    {
      "id": "n1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "> connection.disconnect();\n\nThis is the default api contract in useEffect: useEffect should only return undefined or a function.\n\n[[Hamesh/Sites/react.dev/Lifecycle of Reactive Effects – React#^hm-ncleanup|↗]]",
      "x": -670,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 220
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "> When you looked from the component’s perspective, it was tempting to think of Effects as callbacks.\n\nReact lifecycle advice #1\n\n[[Hamesh/Sites/react.dev/Lifecycle of Reactive Effects – React#^hm-nadvice|↗]]",
      "x": -210,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 220
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "> React starts and stops your Effect one extra time in development\n\nEvery Effect in React development env is done twice\n\n[[Hamesh/Sites/react.dev/Lifecycle of Reactive Effects – React#^hm-ntwice|↗]]",
      "x": 250,
